  "answer_text": "# CFA Institute\n\nHere's an overview of the **CFA Institute**:\n\n## What is CFA Institute?\n\nCFA Institute is a global not-for-profit organization that provides finance education for investment professionals. By promoting the highest standards of ethics, education, and excellence, it helps shape the future of the industry for the ultimate benefit of society.\n\n---\n\n## Key Facts\n\n- **Headquarters:** CFA Institute is headquartered in Charlottesville, Virginia, with additional offices in New York City, Washington, D.C., London, Hong Kong, Mumbai, Beijing, Shanghai, and Abu Dhabi.\n- **Leadership:** The current President and CEO is Margaret Franklin.\n- **Global Reach:** With a heritage of over 75 years, CFA Institute has 200,000 members in 160 locations around the world, providing an unparalleled network of visionary leaders.\n\n---\n\n## History\n\n- In 1947, four financial analyst societies \u2014 Boston, Chicago, New York, and Philadelphia \u2014 cooperated for the purpose of promoting the exchange of ideas and supporting the welfare of their profession, forming the National Federation of Financial Analysts Societies (NFFAS).\n- In 1962, the Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA) designation and code of conduct were established. In 1963, the profession was formalized when 284 candidates sat for the first CFA exam and 268 CFA charters were awarded.\n- In 2004, the Association for Investment Management and Research voted to change its name to CFA Institute.\n\n---\n\n## Programs & Offerings\n\n- The CFA Program is designed to equip candidates with the knowledge and skills necessary to compete and excel in today's complex and evolving investment industry.\n- CFA Institute qualifications and education offerings are designed to support professionals in their practice areas and build confidence with clients and partners.\n- In March 2021, CFA Institute launched the Certificate in ESG Investing due to the high profile of environmental, social, and corporate governance (ESG) factors in socially responsible investing.\n- Its world-class Research & Policy Center offers an unbiased forum for industry leaders, regulators, and subject matter experts to help shape policy and drive positive change.\n\n---\n\n## Recent Developments\n\n- From 2021 onwards, all examinations were shifted to computer-based testing for the three levels of the CFA program.\n\n---\n\nWould you like more specific information about the **CFA exam**, **membership**, **programs**, or anything else related to CFA Institute? \ud83d\ude0a",
